{"findings":[{"file":"services/src/main/java/org/keycloak/authentication/authenticators/browser/UsernameForm.java","line":47,"severity":"critical","category":"bug","title":"Compilation error: isConditionalPasskeysEnabled() is called with no arguments but only the UserModel-taking overload is defined","body":"Line 47 reads `if (context.getUser() != null && !isConditionalPasskeysEnabled()) {`. The only definition added by this PR is `protected boolean isConditionalPasskeysEnabled(UserModel user)` in UsernamePasswordForm.java line 160. There is no no-arg version defined anywhere in the class hierarchy (UsernameForm extends UsernamePasswordForm extends AbstractUsernameFormAuthenticator). The call therefore does not resolve and the module will not compile. The intended logic was likely `!isConditionalPasskeysEnabled(context.getUser())`, mirroring the other call sites in UsernamePasswordForm.authenticate (line 115) and UsernamePasswordForm.challenge (line 137), which both pass `context.getUser()`."},{"file":"services/src/main/java/org/keycloak/authentication/authenticators/browser/WebAuthnAuthenticator.java","line":108,"severity":"medium","category":"bug","title":"IS_USER_IDENTIFIED attribute now depends on shouldShowWebAuthnAuthenticators instead of user != null","body":"Previously, `isUserIdentified` was set to true whenever `context.getUser() != null`. The refactor moved the assignment inside `if (shouldShowWebAuthnAuthenticators(context)) { ... isUserIdentified = true; ... }`. WebAuthnConditionalUIAuthenticator overrides shouldShowWebAuthnAuthenticators to always return false (added in this PR), so IS_USER_IDENTIFIED is always sent as "false" to the form template, including re-authentication scenarios where the user IS identified and a UsernameForm or UsernamePasswordForm authenticator has already hidden the username via USERNAME_HIDDEN. Any template logic that switches on IS_USER_IDENTIFIED (e.g., to label the page, scope the listed passkeys, or render a 're-authenticate as X' state) will behave as if no user is identified. A cleaner fix is to compute `boolean isUserIdentified = user != null;` once and keep the authenticator-list gating inside the if-block, so the two concerns are not coupled."},{"file":"testsuite/integration-arquillian/tests/base/src/test/java/org/keycloak/testsuite/webauthn/passwordless/PasskeysUsernamePasswordFormTest.java","line":291,"severity":"low","category":"test_gap","title":"try/assertThat/fail/catch pattern is misleading and contains dead `fail()` call","body":"The assertion
